[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Temperature"
brief_tooltip = "Warmth drains in cold weather, faster at night.
Shelter and fire reduce cold damage.
Below -40°C is deadly even with gear."
implemented = true
detailed_text = "[b]Cold Is Your Greatest Enemy[/b]

[i]Arctic temperatures on King William Island regularly plunge below -40°C in winter. The Franklin expedition's men, weakened by bad rations and lead poisoning, had little defence against it.[/i]

The colder it gets, the faster your men lose warmth — and the danger rises sharply as temperatures drop. A man caught outside at -40°C with no shelter can freeze to death in hours. At night the cold is even worse.

[b]Staying Warm[/b]

[b]Fire[/b] — The best source of warmth. Keep fires burning near where your men work and rest.
[b]Tents[/b] — Provide steady warmth and cut exposure during storms.
[b]Sunlight[/b] — Daytime provides a small warmth benefit.

Combine these — a tent near a fire is far safer than either alone.

[b]Blizzards[/b]

A heavy blizzard on top of already freezing temperatures can be lethal in the open. Inside a tent, the worst of the storm is blunted. Men caught outside during a blizzard should be recalled immediately.

[b]What to Watch[/b]

• The temperature display in the top-right corner turns blue as conditions worsen
• Build tents and stockpile firewood before winter arrives in December
• Keep everyone sheltered after dark during winter months
• Night is always colder than day — plan outdoor work for daylight hours"
